    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded (`complete: true`).\n\n**Summary: 9 PASS / 10 FAIL**\n\nThe app's core browsing/search, template comparison, scenario tab switching, graph pan/zoom/fit-view/drag, and the risk-gap warning system (creation, display, and clearing) all work correctly.\n\nHowever, testing uncovered a significant, root-cause defect: **every direct per-competency control inside the graph nodes (weight slider, level buttons 1–5, and enable/disable switch) is completely non-functional** — confirmed via multiple independent techniques (mouse drag, click, native DOM `.click()`, keyboard) and contrasted against working identical controls elsewhere in the app. This single defect cascades into failures for FT-4, FT-5, CS-12, IX-13, and IX-20, since none of those requirements can be exercised through the UI.\n\nAdditional independent defects found:\n- **FT-7 / CT-16**: Applying a template or running a scenario simulation updates aggregate metrics/critical-path text but never updates the actual graph nodes' displayed values or \"Critical\" badges, leaving the graph inconsistent with the summary panel.\n- **FT-8**: \"Save Current\" (save-as-template) shows a success toast but has no name/description dialog and persists nothing.\n- **FT-11**: \"Save\" model shows a success toast but has no real persistence — state reverts as soon as you navigate away and back, with no localStorage/sessionStorage usage at all.\n- **IX-19**: Running the initially-selected (Recruitment) scenario without switching tabs produces a \"Simulation Applied\" toast but zero actual metric change, since its default deltas are all 0."
  }
